# 🚀 ClassPlus Backend

> A scalable backend system for assignment management where teachers can create assignments and all students assigned to them receive **real-time notifications**.

---

## 🏗️ System Architecture

```text
                         ┌──────────────┐
                         │   TEACHER    │
                         └──────┬───────┘
                                │
                         Create Assignment
                                │
                                ▼
                     ┌────────────────────┐
                     │ Express Controller │
                     └─────────┬──────────┘
                               │
                 ┌─────────────┴─────────────┐
                 ▼                           ▼
          ┌─────────────┐             ┌──────────────┐
          │   MongoDB   │             │    BullMQ    │
          │  Assignment │             │     Queue    │
          │    Saved    │             └──────┬───────┘
          └─────────────┘                    │
                                             ▼
                                   ┌───────────────────┐
                                   │ Redis Queue       │
                                   │ assignment-       │
                                   │ notification      │
                                   └─────────┬─────────┘
                                             │
                                             ▼
                                   ┌───────────────────┐
                                   │      Worker       │
                                   └─────────┬─────────┘
                                             │
                                  Find Assigned Students
                                             │
                                             ▼
                                   ┌───────────────────┐
                                   │      MongoDB      │
                                   │ Create Notification│
                                   └─────────┬─────────┘
                                             │
                                             ▼
                                   ┌───────────────────┐
                                   │   Redis Pub/Sub   │
                                   └─────────┬─────────┘
                                             │
                                             ▼
                                   ┌───────────────────┐
                                   │    Subscriber     │
                                   └─────────┬─────────┘
                                             │
                                             ▼
                                   ┌───────────────────┐
                                   │     Socket.IO     │
                                   └─────────┬─────────┘
                                             │
                       ┌─────────────────────┼─────────────────────┐
                       ▼                     ▼                     ▼
                 student:S1             student:S2             student:S3
                       │                     │                     │
                       ▼                     ▼                     ▼
                    Student               Student               Student
```

---

## 🔄 How It Works

The complete notification flow is:

```text
Teacher creates assignment
          ↓
Assignment saved in MongoDB
          ↓
BullMQ job added to Redis
          ↓
Worker picks up the job
          ↓
Worker finds students assigned to the teacher
          ↓
Notifications created in MongoDB
          ↓
Notification event published through Redis Pub/Sub
          ↓
Redis Subscriber receives the event
          ↓
Socket.IO emits the notification
          ↓
Students receive the notification in real time
```

---

# 🔌 API Endpoints

## 👨‍🏫 Create Teacher

```http
POST /api/users/teacher
```

Creates a new teacher.

---

## 👨‍🎓 Create Student

```http
POST /api/users/student
```

Creates a new student.

---

## 🔗 Assign Student to Teacher

```http
POST /api/users/assign-student
```

Associates a student with a teacher.

---

## 📝 Create Assignment

```http
POST /api/assignments
```

### Request Body

```json
{
  "teacherId": "TEACHER_ID",
  "title": "Operating Systems Assignment",
  "description": "Explain process scheduling",
  "dueDate": "2026-09-25"
}
```

When an assignment is created, a background notification job is added to the BullMQ queue.

---

# 🔔 Real-Time Notifications

Students connect to the server using **Socket.IO** and join their individual rooms:

```text
student:<studentId>
```

For example:

```text
student:64abc123
```

When a new assignment is created, the server emits:

```text
new-assignment
```

Only the students assigned to that teacher receive the notification.

---

# ⚙️ Tech Stack

| Technology         | Purpose                          |
| ------------------ | -------------------------------- |
| **Node.js**        | Backend runtime                  |
| **Express.js**     | REST API                         |
| **MongoDB**        | Persistent data storage          |
| **Redis**          | Queue and Pub/Sub infrastructure |
| **BullMQ**         | Background job processing        |
| **Socket.IO**      | Real-time communication          |
| **Docker**         | Containerization                 |
| **Docker Compose** | Multi-container development      |

---

# 🧠 Core Concepts

```text
BullMQ
   → Handles background jobs

Redis
   → Stores queue data and handles Pub/Sub

Worker
   → Processes notification jobs

Redis Pub/Sub
   → Communicates notification events

Socket.IO
   → Delivers real-time notifications

MongoDB
   → Stores assignments, users and notifications

Docker
   → Provides isolated application environments
```

---

# 🐳 Docker Setup

Docker Compose runs the main backend services:

```text
┌──────────────────────┐
│        Docker        │
│                      │
│  ┌───────┐  ┌──────┐│
│  │  API  │  │Worker││
│  └───┬───┘  └──┬───┘│
│      │          │    │
│      └────┬─────┘    │
│           │          │
│       ┌───▼───┐      │
│       │ Redis │      │
│       └───────┘      │
└──────────────────────┘

        +
    MongoDB Atlas
```

MongoDB can be hosted separately using **MongoDB Atlas**.

---

# 🚀 Getting Started

## 1. Clone the Repository

```bash
git clone <your-repository-url>
cd classplus-api
```

## 2. Install Dependencies

```bash
npm install
```

## 3. Configure Environment Variables

Create a `.env` file:

```env
PORT=5000
MONGO_URI=your_mongodb_uri
REDIS_HOST=redis
REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379
```

## 4. Run Using Docker

```bash
docker compose up --build
```

The API, worker and Redis services will start together.

---

## 💻 Run Without Docker

Start the API:

```bash
node server.js
```

Start the BullMQ worker separately:

```bash
node bullmq/notification.worker.js
```

Make sure Redis and MongoDB are running locally or use a hosted MongoDB instance.

